{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"alias":"brusque-curious-pomeranian","creation_channel":"python","description":"## Context\nREADME installation prose has stale dependency versions and ambiguous Git requirements. `pyproject.toml` defines the package contract. `pugnacious-soaplike-blackfish` records the decision to enforce Git 2.38 for development and CI without test skips.\n\n## Plan\n- Document the three base dependencies.\n- Correct the MCP extra to `mcp>=1.28.1,<2` with PyJWT cryptography support.\n- Describe Anthropic, Bedrock, OpenAI, and Google provider installation accurately.\n- State that Git is a runtime prerequisite.\n- State that Git 2.38 is the development and test floor and that the S3 repair path also needs `merge-tree --write-tree`.\n- Change documentation only. Do not modify packaging.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [x] README dependency claims match `pyproject.toml`.\n- [x] Provider-extra guidance names the correct installation boundary for each provider.\n- [x] Git guidance preserves the enforced contributor and CI floor without presenting it as a universal floor for every runtime path.\n- [x] The S3 repair capability requirement remains discoverable.\n- [x] Targeted README and documentation checks pass.\n- [x] No dependency declaration or packaging file changes.","id":"2fec-767c-2829-4fc6","parent_id":"e867-0f39-b887-40fa","priority":2,"tags":[],"ticket_type":"story","title":"F08B correct README installation contracts"},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"CREATE","timestamp":1788161042719336001,"uuid":"bb1df2c6-6120-4662-80c2-4f4bb0257770"}